| `Hosted` asks whether another program is holding this one. Run on its own,
| in either output mode, the answer is no — and for `code run` it is always
| no, because an interpreted program can never be a guest.
|
| The yes side needs a host, so it lives in `tests/hosted_app.rs`.

emit Hosted {} to core get where
assert where ∈ HostedResult
assert where._class = "HostedResult"
assert where.value ∈ Boolean
assert not where.value

| The bare form means the same thing.
emit Hosted to core get again
assert not again.value

| It is a value like any other, so it can steer a decision.
let door = "net_server"
if where.value { door = "membrane" }
assert door = "net_server"
